---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Design" description="How Clessidra works: signal path, recording, density, grains, slices, level, with the firmware's values.">

<h1>Design</h1>
<p class="lead">How the firmware works. Every value is the firmware's.</p>

<h2 class="label" id="signal-path">Signal Path</h2>
<ol class="panel rows path">
  <li class="row"><span class="label">01 Input</span><span>Left and right summed to mono, DC removed</span></li>
  <li class="row"><span class="label">02 Ring</span><span>Always listening, 31 s</span></li>
  <li class="row"><span class="label">03 Buffers</span><span>Two of 30 s, mono, 48 kHz. P11 fills the one not playing</span></li>
  <li class="row"><span class="label">04 Grains</span><span>32 voices, up to 131 grains per second</span></li>
  <li class="row"><span class="label">05 Normaliser</span><span>Back to the input's level</span></li>
  <li class="row"><span class="label">06 Reverb</span><span>Follows Density</span></li>
  <li class="row"><span class="label">07 Mix</span><span>Dry and wet, equal power</span></li>
  <li class="row"><span class="label">08 Limiter</span><span>Look-ahead 5 ms, ceiling −0.5 dBFS</span></li>
  <li class="row"><span class="label">09 Output</span><span>Stereo</span></li>
</ol>

<h2 class="label" id="record">Record</h2>
<div class="prose">
  <p>The input goes into a ring all the time. P11 takes from it into the buffer that isn't playing, then plays it. Grains playing finish on the old recording, new ones start on the new: no click, and no grain ever reads sound being written.</p>
</div>
<div class="panel table"><table>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Tap</td><td>Under 0.3 s: the 8 s before the touch</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Hold</td><td>From 50 ms before the touch to the release. Longer than 30 s keeps the last 30 s</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Trim</td><td>Silence below −60 dBFS cut at both ends, 5 ms kept. A silent recording changes nothing</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Landing</td><td>Copied at 21 times real time: 30 s in 1.4 s</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Selection</td><td>Between Start (S30) and End (S35), in either order</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>

<h2 class="label" id="density">Density</h2>
<div class="prose">
  <p>One fader, from single drops to a cloud. Grain size, window and reverb follow it. Size (S31) moves the grain size 2 octaves either way, and a firm press on a slice raises it.</p>
</div>
<div class="panel table"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Fader</th><th class="num">Grains/s</th><th class="num">Grain</th><th>Window</th><th class="num">Reverb</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Under 2 %</td><td class="num">Closed</td><td class="num">–</td><td>–</td><td class="num">Rings out</td></tr>
    <tr><td>2 %</td><td class="num">0.3</td><td class="num">31 ms</td><td>Percussive</td><td class="num">5.4 s</td></tr>
    <tr><td>25 %</td><td class="num">1.3</td><td class="num">53 ms</td><td>Percussive</td><td class="num">3.5 s</td></tr>
    <tr><td>50 %</td><td class="num">5.9</td><td class="num">95 ms</td><td>Towards Hann</td><td class="num">2.2 s</td></tr>
    <tr><td>75 %</td><td class="num">28</td><td class="num">169 ms</td><td>Hann</td><td class="num">1.4 s</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Top</td><td class="num">131</td><td class="num">300 ms</td><td>Hann</td><td class="num">0.8 s</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>
<p class="caption after">Grains per second rise exponentially. Reverb is its decay time, and its share of the sound falls as Density rises. From 60 % the grains start to differ by themselves, up to Scatter at 0.3 at the top.</p>
