<h2 class="label" id="grain">A Grain</h2>
<div class="panel table"><table>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Position</td><td>The playhead's point, plus Scatter's reach: up to ±2 s, cubic. Stays inside what is playing, mirrored at its ends</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Pitch</td><td>S33. With S09 on, random pitch grows with Scatter: whole octaves or free, most grains near the pitch, a few up to ±24 semitones</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Size</td><td>Density and S31, 10 ms to half the sound, at most 4 s. With Scatter, each from half to twice</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Window</td><td>From Density: percussive to Hann</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Pan</td><td>Equal power. The width grows with the grains sounding and with Scatter</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Direction</td><td>The playhead's</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Duration</td><td>The same at any pitch</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>

<h2 class="label" id="starts">Starts and Voices</h2>
<div class="panel table"><table>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Starts</td><td>Grains per second, whatever their size. Scatter at 0: periodic. Up: random intervals, without the closest starts and the longest gaps, at the same mean</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Voices</td><td>32. Over 24 sounding, the one furthest along fades out in 5 ms, so a new grain always starts</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Overlap</td><td>At high density the grains shorten, so 24 voices hold whole windows: 183 ms at the top of Density</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>

<h2 class="label" id="slices">Slices</h2>
<div class="prose">
  <p>Each new recording is cut into 7 slices at its onsets: a rise of 6 dB over the 30 ms before, in 5 ms frames, above −50 dBFS, at least 50 ms apart. The strongest onsets are kept, and each slice starts 5 ms before its onset. With too few onsets, the longest slices are halved.</p>
  <p>P03–P09 play the slices, first to last: left to right on the panel, top to bottom within a column. A touch plays one from its start. A firm press raises Density towards the top. Released, the whole selection plays again, once a one-shot has finished its slice.</p>
</div>

<h2 class="label" id="speed">Speed and Mode</h2>
<div class="panel table"><table>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Speed</td><td>Centre stops. Up forward, down backward. Speed rises with the square of the distance: 1 halfway, with a detent, 4 at the end. Crossing the centre flips</td></tr>
    <tr><td>One-shot</td><td>S07 (Mode) up. Stops at the end of the selection or slice, until a slice or a flip restarts it</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Ping-pong</td><td>S07 centre. Turns at each end</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Loop</td><td>S07 down. Wraps round</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>

<h2 class="label" id="level">Level</h2>
<div class="panel table"><table>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Normaliser</td><td>Copies of one sound add up in amplitude, independent grains in power. Both are measured, smoothed over 5 ms, and the sum is brought back to the input's level with 0.9 headroom. Grains that cancel are not boosted</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Limiter</td><td>+6 dB in. Look-ahead 5 ms, ceiling −0.5 dBFS</td></tr>
    <tr><td>LED</td><td>Glows with the grains. A 300 ms pulse when a control reaches its centre</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>

<h2 class="label" id="runtime">Runtime</h2>
<div class="panel table"><table>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Board</td><td>Daisy Seed. 48 kHz, 48-sample blocks (1 ms). Pads read every 3 ms</td></tr>
    <tr><td>CPU</td><td>16 % closed, 76 % at the heaviest settings, measured on the board</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Browser</td><td>The same code, compiled to WebAssembly. 48 kHz, 128-sample blocks, controls read once per block</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>
</Base>
